{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghQT1AZhg5jr8vw5YF6v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Result: Dq ≈ 407 cm⁻¹ (Δt = 10Dq ≈ 4070 cm⁻¹) and B ≈ 748 cm⁻¹. C is not determined by these bands.**\n\n**Method.** A tetrahedral d⁷ ion has the same spin-allowed energy-level pattern as an octahedral d³ ion. The ground term is ⁴A₂, and the Dq sign is reversed. I therefore fitted the three bands with the d³ Tanabe–Sugano model.\n\n**Assignments.**\n- ν₁ = 4070 cm⁻¹ is ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₂(F). In this model ν₁ equals 10Dq, which fixes Dq.\n- ν₂ = 7030 cm⁻¹ is ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₁(F).\n- ν₃ = 16400 cm⁻¹ is ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₁(P).\n\n**Fit quality.** The predicted bands are 4068, 7031 and 16400 cm⁻¹. The RMSE is about 1.2 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Covalency.** B ≈ 748 cm⁻¹ is about 0.67 of the free-ion Co²⁺ value, which I took as roughly 1115 cm⁻¹ from memory. That indicates moderate covalency, which is reasonable for a tetrahedral Co(II) complex.\n\n**C.** The spin-allowed bands barely depend on C. The tool's output of C = 4133 cm⁻¹ is a default value carried through the fit, not a fitted result, so I am not reporting it as a determined parameter.\n\n{\"Dq\": 407, \"B\": 748, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Tetrahedral d7 maps onto the octahedral d3 diagram; the three spin-allowed bands fit with RMSE about 1 cm^-1, and C is not constrained by them.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2828,"cache_read_input_tokens":7974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2828,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4cbb0c0-79d3-40bb-ad66-df8955ee2735","uuid":"a2489abc-8535-4ced-9590-c0e4c0a76b79","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:21:14.982Z","request_i